.SH "NAME"
pcre2_compile_context_create \- create a compile context
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
.fam C
#include <pcre2.h>

pcre2_compile_context *pcre2_compile_context_create(
      pcre2_general_context *gcontext);
.fam
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function creates and initializes a new compile context. If its argument is
NULL, \f(CRmalloc()\fP is used to get the necessary memory; otherwise the memory
allocation function within the general context is used. The result is NULL if
the memory could not be obtained.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.